WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.094
Step 1. Open the encounter.

1.2
00:00:02.094 --> 00:00:07.011
You mark an allergy as entered in error when it was recorded by mistake.

1.3
00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:12.018
On the Encounters tab, select View Encounter on an open encounter.

2.1
00:00:12.018 --> 00:00:17.676
Step 2. Open the allergy form. In the Allergies panel, select the Edit pencil.

2.2
00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:21.296
The form shows the patient's saved allergies.

3.1
00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:23.329
Step 3. Find the allergy.

3.2
00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:28.608
Each allergy is a row, and the Substance column shows the allergen.

4.1
00:00:28.608 --> 00:00:32.028
Step 4. Mark the allergy as entered in error.

4.2
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:36.607
Open the row menu with the three dots, and select Remove Allergy.

4.3
00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:40.278
The row's Status changes to Entered in Error.

5.1
00:00:40.278 --> 00:00:43.631
Step 5. Save the form. Select Save Changes.

5.2
00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:48.249
Care keeps the allergy, but leaves it out of every allergy list,

5.3
00:00:48.249 --> 00:00:51.780
so the Allergies panel no longer shows it.
